Turn completed.
1. Work performed: In [single_token_forward_model.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/api/single_token_forward_model.cpp#L39) I added VRAM-budget helpers, `NEMOTRON_FORWARD_VRAM_RESERVE_MB` parsing with a `512 MiB` default, and request-context byte estimation. In [single_token_forward_model.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/api/single_token_forward_model.cpp#L563) I now sample `cudaMemGetInfo()` at `Create()` start and again after all layer slices are built, store the post-weight free bytes on the model impl, and in [single_token_forward_model.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/api/single_token_forward_model.cpp#L801) cap `max_tokens`, `scratch_tokens`, and `attention_total_pages` before `RequestExecutionContext::Create()`. I also logged the checkpoint in [PLAN.md](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/proj-2026-04-01-1534/PLAN.md#L357).

2. How VRAM is now measured and used: `Create()` measures initial free/total VRAM before any uploads, keeps the existing weight upload order, then measures free/total VRAM again after all weights are resident. `CreateRequestContext()` uses that stored post-weight free VRAM minus the reserve headroom to bound per-request allocations; if the original request budget is too large, it shrinks the KV-cache page count and token capacity to what fits in the measured remainder, and fails early if even a 1-token context would exceed the measured budget.

3. Compile status: `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4 2>&1 | tail -5` passed, and `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target full_forward_manifest_smoke_test -j4 2>&1 | tail -5` passed.

4. Concerns: this is still a per-request cap derived from the stored post-weight snapshot, so multiple simultaneously live request contexts are not globally coordinated yet. The sizing is shape-based rather than allocator-aware, so fragmentation beyond the explicit reserve can still matter.

CHECKPOINT: 4
